# Joo Dee, One of Many: "then sacrifice an artifact or creature" is any artifact, not only a creature. Bot1 sacrifices Mox Ruby,
# keeping both Joo Dees (the original tapped, the copy untapped and summoning-sick); the surveil keeps the Mountain on top
# (CR 701.25a), and the {B} was paid exactly by Mox Jet, which is not tapped again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Joo Dee, One of Many
Swamp x4
Mountain
Mountain
Plains x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Joo Dee, One of Many.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Joo Dee, One of Many.Activate
Bot1.Arrange(Mountain |)
Bot1.Choose(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby)
? Bot1.Mana =

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Ruby
Bot1.Battlefield = Joo Dee, One of Many; Joo Dee, One of Many; Mox Jet
Bot1.Battlefield.Joo Dee, One of Many#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Joo Dee, One of Many#2.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Joo Dee, One of Many#2.SummoningSick = true
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
